{"id": "EUVD-2026-103663", "enisaUuid": "f511c013-244a-33fa-9cd6-48f8b9009066", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\neth: fbnic: Handle maximum standalone channels\n\nStandalone channels use one NAPI vector for each Tx and Rx queue.\nfbnic's allocation path excludes FBNIC_MAX_TXQS from that layout. A\n64-Tx/64-Rx configuration therefore records 128 vectors but allocates\nonly 64, leaving NULL entries that resource setup dereferences.\n\nInclude the maximum vector count in standalone allocation.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:46", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9843e5fabd6ab296df9c025b1d0e5bf79a6b8a08", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6c903188b67617070017305a325fa326f270a43d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16ff1023213cc39c1a7ce737205c2a1a53c3a716", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1f4c73064a50f53d596c6f1d06d2d700f43c4b32"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qp9r-4gxq-qwmm", "CVE-2026-98618"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "41eb34cc-2f50-3269-9ad2-951fd9909169", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "488c69eb-37d8-370d-83e6-6187db8ab58b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bc6107771bb4be3009168cfda24d22131c026fe8 <1f4c73064a50f53d596c6f1d06d2d700f43c4b32"}, {"id": "9b5f8c3f-ccd4-39b6-9c8f-34f2265cb949", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a7d67340-fe6a-317e-a7e8-e41bff61a300", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a952a8c3-f91f-3432-9ed7-6e8c265bc032", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bc6107771bb4be3009168cfda24d22131c026fe8 <9843e5fabd6ab296df9c025b1d0e5bf79a6b8a08"}, {"id": "b4d7042b-ad01-3dfa-a8ff-b75ea809470b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"n